<title>CHINA: China starts vegetable oil plant with Cyprus firm.</title>
<headline>China starts vegetable oil plant with Cyprus firm.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has started work on a 150 million yuan ($18.1 million) vegetable oil plant with a company from Cyprus, the Xinhua news agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Inner Mongolia Vegetable Oil Refinery and a Cypriot technology trading company were building the new Meng-Sai Vegetable Oil Refinery in Hohhot in northern Inner Mongolia, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>The new refinery would handle 330 tonnes of raw material a day and generate 66 million yuan in profits on sales of 380 million yuan a year, it said.</p>
<p>Xinhua gave no further details.</p>
</text>
